# Month 3 — AWS Foundation Final Revision

## 1. Cloud Computing & AWS Basics

- Cloud Computing → Internet ke through computing resources/services use karna.
- AWS → Amazon Web Services, cloud platform.
- EC2 → Cloud-based virtual server / compute.
- S3 → Object storage.
- CloudWatch → Monitoring and observability.

## 2. IAM — Identity & Access Management

- IAM → AWS identities aur permissions manage karta hai.
- IAM User → Identity.
- IAM Policy → Permissions define karti hai.
- IAM Group → Multiple users ka collection.
- IAM Role → Permissions wali identity jo users/services/resources assume kar sakte hain.
- Least Privilege → Sirf required permissions dena.

Important Difference:
- IAM Policy → AWS actions/resources ki permissions control karti hai.
- Security Group → Network traffic/ports control karta hai.

## 3. EC2 — Elastic Compute Cloud

EC2 = AWS cloud-based virtual server.

Important Components:
- AMI → OS/software setup ka template/image.
- Instance Type → CPU, memory aur compute resources.
- Key Pair → Secure SSH authentication.
- Security Group → Network traffic control.
- Public IP → Internet-facing connectivity.
- Private IP → Private network communication.

Common Ports:
- SSH → 22
- HTTP → 80
- HTTPS → 443

## 4. SSH + EC2 Web Server

SSH = Secure Shell.

SSH ka use remote EC2 Linux server ko securely access/manage karne ke liye hota hai.

Flow:
Laptop → Internet → EC2 Public IP → Security Group Port 22 → SSH → EC2 Linux

Web Server:
Internet → EC2 → Security Group Port 80/443 → Web Server → Website

## 5. Amazon S3

S3 = Simple Storage Service.

- Bucket → Files/objects store karne ka container.
- Object → Actual stored file.
- Object Key → Object ka name/path.

Static Website:
- index.html
- style.css
- script.js

S3 Versioning:
- Same object ke previous versions preserve kiye ja sakte hain.

S3 Lifecycle:
- Objects ko time/rules ke according automatically manage kar sakta hai.

S3 Security:
- IAM Policies
- Bucket Policies
- Block Public Access
- Encryption

## 6. CloudFront

CloudFront = CDN (Content Delivery Network).

CloudFront edge locations ke through content ko users ke closer deliver karne mein help karta hai.

Flow:
S3 → CloudFront → Edge Locations → Users

- S3 → Storage
- CloudFront → Content Delivery

## 7. CloudWatch

CloudWatch AWS resources/applications ki monitoring aur observability ke liye use hota hai.

Important:
- Metrics
- Logs
- Alarms

Example:
EC2 → CloudWatch → CPU Metric → Alarm → Notification/Action

## 8. AWS CLI

AWS CLI = AWS Command Line Interface.

AWS CLI ek command-line tool hai, AWS service nahi.

WSL/Terminal se AWS resources ko manage/interact kar sakte hain.

Examples:
aws s3 ls
aws s3 cp file.txt s3://bucket-name/
aws ec2 describe-instances

DevOps Connection:
AWS CLI → Commands → Scripts → Automation

## 9. Application Load Balancer — ALB

ALB = Application Load Balancer.

ALB incoming HTTP/HTTPS requests ko multiple healthy targets ke beech distribute karta hai.

Flow:
Users → ALB → EC2 + EC2

Purpose:
- Traffic distribution
- Multiple EC2 targets
- Health checks
- HTTP/HTTPS application routing

